# pm-kit.conf — instance configuration for the cellarman PM work-companion.
# Copy next to your claude-brain/pm-kit/ directory as `pm-kit.conf`.
# Sourced by pm-kit/doctor.sh and pm-kit/load-telemetry.sh AFTER they set:
#   REPO_ROOT — the repo root (parent of claude-brain/)
#   KIT_DIR   — the pm-kit/ directory
# Paths here may use those variables. Zero project knowledge lives in the kit
# scripts; everything instance-specific lives HERE.

# The always-read index the PM loads on every invocation.
PM_INDEX="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/agents/acme-pm-memory.md"

# The lazy-loaded topic corpus.
PM_MEMORY_DIR="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/agents/acme-pm-memory"

# Agent definition: canonical (git-synced) vs installed (what Claude Code loads).
PM_AGENT_CANONICAL="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/agents/acme-pm.md"
PM_AGENT_INSTALLED="$HOME/.claude/agents/acme-pm.md"

# Index byte budget. Start here for a new project; raise only when the HEALTHY
# one-liner floor demands it (many mature arcs), never to accommodate
# narration. The budget bounds DRIFT, not routing.
#
# 🔴 CALIBRATE FAIL AGAINST THE TOKEN READ CAP, NOT AGAINST BYTES ALONE.
# The constraint that actually binds is the reader's token cap (~25 000 tokens
# for Claude Code's Read tool): an oversized index does not error — it returns
# a successful-looking PARTIAL read, and what falls off is the BOTTOM of the
# file (the routing table). Token density varies with composition and drifts
# between passes (a dense, emoji-heavy corpus measured 0.53–0.54 tok/byte,
# putting the one-pass wall at ~46 KB — under the default FAIL below). The
# test, not the count: Read the index and check for a "lines X-Y of N" partial
# banner; set PM_BUDGET_FAIL below the wall YOUR corpus measures. An index the
# agent cannot read whole is a hard failure, not drift.
PM_BUDGET_WARN=49152    # 48 KB
PM_BUDGET_FAIL=65536    # 64 KB

# Optional: where pm-kit/catalog.sh writes the derived card catalog of the
# topic corpus (default: pm-catalog.tsv next to the index). Gitignore it —
# it is derived on demand and embeds the per-machine load telemetry.
# PM_CATALOG="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/agents/pm-catalog.tsv"

# A single index line longer than this is narration, not routing.
PM_LINE_WARN=1536

# More dated blockquotes ("> **YYYY-...") than this in the index = journal
# entries accumulating where they don't belong.
PM_DATED_WARN=3

# Per-machine load-telemetry log (gitignore it — the dormancy signal is
# per-developer by design).
PM_LOAD_LOG="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/agents/.pm-load-log.tsv"

# Days after which a topic file with zero recorded loads is flagged dormant.
PM_DORMANT_DAYS=90

# Size past which a single topic file is doing a DIRECTORY's job and should be
# split into per-subtopic files + a small pointer index.
#
# This threshold can exist in doctrine and be enforced by nobody — the index
# budget above measures the INDEX alone, so the topic corpus can drift
# unwatched for a long time. It surfaces only when someone manually measures a
# topic file and finds it far past the threshold. Unlike the index budget this
# is WARN only: an oversized topic file costs nothing per consult (it is
# lazy-loaded) — it costs when you must read or edit it whole. Hence no FAIL
# tier.
PM_TOPIC_WARN=81920    # 80 KB

# Verbatim pre-compaction snapshots of the index. They are a safety net, not a
# store: git already holds every one of them (`git show <sha>:<index path>`),
# so past a handful they are pure duplication that no other check can see —
# the topic-size check above weighs the index alone, and the orphan check
# never calls them orphans because the archive README references them.
# Unset PM_ARCHIVE_DIR to skip the check entirely.
PM_ARCHIVE_DIR="$PM_MEMORY_DIR/index-relocated-detail"
PM_ARCHIVE_GLOB="index-verbatim-*.md"
PM_ARCHIVE_MAX=3

# ── Skill mirror (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment if your project publishes the LIVE Claude Code skill store into a
# repo-tracked mirror via a one-directional publish/sync step (copy live →
# repo, never merge). In that shape, an edit made directly to the MIRROR is
# invisible work: the next publish silently overwrites it from live, and the
# loss appears only as a net-deletion hunk buried inside a batch of additions.
# The tell is DIRECTION, not difference: mirror content that live does not
# have is the signal, not a byte-for-byte diff.
# PM_SKILLS_LIVE="$HOME/.claude/skills"
# PM_SKILLS_MIRROR="$REPO_ROOT/claude-brain/skills"
